The compiler sources are now `destiny.*`, and the library is now `libfate`

The last `dmd` and Phobos names visible to users and contributors are gone.

$(UL
$(LI The compiler sources moved from `compiler/src/dmd/` to
`compiler/src/destiny/`, and their modules from `dmd.*` to `destiny.*`
(for example `destiny.funcsem`). The C++ headers moved from
`compiler/include/dmd/` to `compiler/include/destiny/`, and their namespace
from `dmd` to `destiny`. Code using the compiler as a library must update its
imports.)
$(LI The compiler links with `libfate` by default instead of `libphobos2`
(`fate64.lib` / `fate32mscoff.lib` on Windows). Pass `-defaultlib=libfate.so`
instead of `-defaultlib=libphobos2.so` to link with the shared library.)
$(LI The build target is `destiny` (`./build.d destiny`; `make destiny` as
before), and the man page is `destiny.1`.)
$(LI Help text and error messages name `destiny`, for example
"run `destiny -man` to open browser on manual".)
$(LI In the test suite, the compiler under test is `$DESTINY` instead of
`$DMD`, in shell and dshell tests and in test output.)
)

Kept: upstream citations, the upstream host compiler (`HOST_DC`,
`dmd-2.113.1`), internal build identifiers, and the `-Xi=compilerInfo`
interface value `dmd`.
